1
00:01:39,480 --> 00:01:40,677
Do you like it?

2
00:01:41,478 --> 00:01:43,419
You son of a bitch!

3
00:01:43,419 --> 00:01:44,774
Why did you lie to me?

4
00:01:44,774 --> 00:01:46,551
Why did you lie to me?

5
00:01:46,551 --> 00:01:52,112
I'm not some random person
whom you can fool with your campaign!

6
00:01:52,112 --> 00:01:55,575
Your family would smile at me,
but in fact, you all look down on me!

7
00:01:55,575 --> 00:01:59,407
You act so high and mighty,
but you're such an asshole!

8
00:02:04,566 --> 00:02:06,080
I'm sorry?

9
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:07,881
Fuck you!

10
00:02:10,091 --> 00:02:11,636
Eva?

11
00:02:12,520 --> 00:02:14,144
Eva?

12
00:02:15,184 --> 00:02:16,847
Eva!

13
00:02:29,174 --> 00:02:30,742
I'm sorry.

14
00:02:38,043 --> 00:02:42,710
I should have been
more understanding and supportive,

15
00:02:42,710 --> 00:02:44,352
about you and Grandma.

16
00:02:49,462 --> 00:02:53,864
You can rest assured
that Nicole and I are just friends.

17
00:02:53,864 --> 00:02:57,200
There's no one in my heart but you.

18
00:03:03,430 --> 00:03:05,360
Are you still mad at me?

19
00:03:06,950 --> 00:03:09,808
If something is bothering you, we can talk.

20
00:03:09,808 --> 00:03:11,640
Please say something.

21
00:03:14,022 --> 00:03:15,668
The other day...

22
00:03:17,430 --> 00:03:21,160
an officer asked Domino about you and Ginny.

23
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:22,961
An officer?

24
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:26,869
That's strange.

25
00:03:28,080 --> 00:03:32,378
I saw him in front of the hospital,
and he said nothing.

26
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:37,109
Do you know what he asked her about?

27
00:03:38,126 --> 00:03:42,360
When you were in the US,
it was the same time as when Ginny was there.

28
00:03:44,127 --> 00:03:45,647
And?

29
00:03:47,120 --> 00:03:50,040
So what? What's the matter?

30
00:03:50,758 --> 00:03:53,840
Many people in my parties visited the US
at the same time.

31
00:03:54,840 --> 00:03:57,640
The officer needed to question everyone,
don't you think so?

32
00:04:02,230 --> 00:04:06,094
Come on, he was just doing his job
and I helped him.

33
00:04:06,094 --> 00:04:08,440
I have nothing to hide anyway.

34
00:04:10,920 --> 00:04:12,920
Don't worry about me.

35
00:04:17,843 --> 00:04:21,500
Excuse me, I think I should go.

36
00:04:22,938 --> 00:04:27,118
I kept her company
while Domino was running some errands.

37
00:04:27,118 --> 00:04:28,259
Sure, feel free to leave.

38
00:04:28,259 --> 00:04:29,521
Okay.

39
00:04:32,824 --> 00:04:34,404
Wait.

40
00:04:37,235 --> 00:04:39,688
I think I need to practice more.

41
00:04:39,688 --> 00:04:41,326
I feel like I didn't do well enough.

42
00:04:43,432 --> 00:04:44,678
Sure.

43
00:04:44,678 --> 00:04:46,305
Eva.

44
00:04:47,392 --> 00:04:50,160
But I'm here to take you to dinner.

45
00:04:51,110 --> 00:04:53,123
I'm not free today.

46
00:04:53,123 --> 00:04:55,560
I have a lot to do.

47
00:04:58,360 --> 00:05:00,904
- Let's do this.
- Sure.

48
00:05:00,904 --> 00:05:02,705
Sorry about that.

49
00:05:24,673 --> 00:05:26,689
Were you okay earlier?

50
00:05:30,040 --> 00:05:32,160
Why are you asking me this?

51
00:05:32,782 --> 00:05:37,320
Nothing. You just looked so tense earlier,
when...

52
00:05:39,795 --> 00:05:41,324
Never mind.

53
00:05:59,080 --> 00:06:02,616
Do you want to practice, or...

54
00:06:03,403 --> 00:06:05,240
you just want to be alone?

55
00:06:09,496 --> 00:06:11,760
I'll go and sit over there.

56
00:06:12,787 --> 00:06:14,640
Let me know when you feel better.

57
00:06:20,715 --> 00:06:21,970
Hey.

58
00:06:23,280 --> 00:06:24,887
Take your time.

59
00:07:49,256 --> 00:07:53,486
What's the matter? Why are you so quiet?

60
00:07:58,403 --> 00:08:00,204
Hey! Hey!

61
00:08:01,100 --> 00:08:02,901
What's wrong?

62
00:08:04,027 --> 00:08:07,640
Eva, what is it?

63
00:08:16,798 --> 00:08:19,240
Are you still mad at Wee?

64
00:08:27,846 --> 00:08:29,320
What?

65
00:08:34,798 --> 00:08:36,342
Is this...

66
00:08:41,261 --> 00:08:44,463
Book said that I should know about this.

67
00:08:44,463 --> 00:08:47,467
So, are you going to see her?

68
00:08:47,467 --> 00:08:49,594
I am.

69
00:08:49,594 --> 00:08:51,723
I'm so furious.

70
00:08:51,723 --> 00:08:56,200
But I kept quiet about this,
because I want to know more from Book first.

71
00:09:01,837 --> 00:09:05,900
Hey, I... I need to confess something.

72
00:09:07,560 --> 00:09:09,086
What?

73
00:09:09,086 --> 00:09:12,720
I also heard about Wee's behavior.

74
00:09:15,560 --> 00:09:16,886
About?

75
00:09:17,824 --> 00:09:20,123
I also heard that he was dating someone else.

76
00:09:20,123 --> 00:09:23,080
But I had no idea it was Ginny.

77
00:09:24,027 --> 00:09:26,680
Why didn't you tell me?

78
00:09:30,472 --> 00:09:32,350
Eva.

79
00:09:35,299 --> 00:09:37,838
You're not stupid.

80
00:09:37,838 --> 00:09:40,960
You chose to ignore it, didn't you?

81
00:09:44,355 --> 00:09:46,500
And I had no evidence.

82
00:09:46,500 --> 00:09:49,280
If I had told you, you would be mad at me.

83
00:09:56,190 --> 00:09:57,619
What's next?

84
00:09:58,443 --> 00:10:00,776
What are you going to do?

85
00:10:08,590 --> 00:10:10,260
I decided to stay with him...

86
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:15,000
Because I always believed
that he was loyal to me.

87
00:10:16,040 --> 00:10:18,080
And that he loved only me.

88
00:10:22,077 --> 00:10:24,120
I will go and meet Book.

89
00:10:24,840 --> 00:10:27,368
I'll ask her about Ginny's trip to New York

90
00:10:27,368 --> 00:10:29,280
and compare it with Wee's trip schedule.

91
00:10:31,390 --> 00:10:34,190
If I'm certain that he had cheated on me,

92
00:10:35,016 --> 00:10:36,920
I will break up with him.

93
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:10,273
<i>This is weird for me,</i>

94
00:11:10,273 --> 00:11:16,680
<i>to see another me standing right here
and staring back at me.</i>

95
00:11:25,771 --> 00:11:27,270
Hey.

96
00:11:27,270 --> 00:11:29,883
What? I didn't watch anything.

97
00:11:33,320 --> 00:11:34,904
What do you mean?

98
00:11:34,904 --> 00:11:37,475
It's late, you should go to bed.

99
00:11:37,475 --> 00:11:39,742
So you can recover faster. Okay?

100
00:11:43,678 --> 00:11:47,144
It's not that late. It's only 8 PM.

101
00:11:53,843 --> 00:11:56,680
<i>Hello, Book? Where should we meet?</i>

102
00:11:56,680 --> 00:11:58,680
<i>We need to talk in the car.</i>

103
00:11:58,680 --> 00:12:00,552
<i>I don't want anyone to find out
that we had met up.</i>

104
00:12:00,552 --> 00:12:02,320
<i>It is that bad?</i>

105
00:12:02,320 --> 00:12:04,720
<i>You need to see it yourself,
and you'll understand.</i>

106
00:12:30,784 --> 00:12:34,371
I got this package from someone
after Ginny passed away.

107
00:12:34,371 --> 00:12:36,560
They rang the bell and just dropped it off.

108
00:12:49,240 --> 00:12:51,720
Did you know that it was Wee?

109
00:12:53,283 --> 00:12:55,587
Ginny said that she dated a politician,

110
00:12:55,587 --> 00:12:58,160
but it was seven to eight months ago.

111
00:13:01,859 --> 00:13:05,320
Do you know who sent you these?

112
00:13:06,427 --> 00:13:08,800
If I were to guess,

113
00:13:08,800 --> 00:13:12,360
I think it was her stalker who attacked you.

114
00:13:13,720 --> 00:13:16,592
He was stalking her
even before she was famous.

115
00:13:16,592 --> 00:13:18,971
He knew everything about Ginny,

116
00:13:18,971 --> 00:13:22,160
and used to dig up Ginny's trash
in front of her house.

117
00:13:22,160 --> 00:13:27,600
He hired a photographer who lived there
to take these photos for him.

118
00:13:29,267 --> 00:13:32,254
Can I keep these photos?

119
00:13:32,254 --> 00:13:35,054
I'm going to burn them after this.
Why do you need them for?

120
00:13:35,054 --> 00:13:38,720
If the photos are leaked,
we all will be in big trouble.

121
00:13:40,158 --> 00:13:42,024
Honestly,

122
00:13:42,024 --> 00:13:45,640
if I had known that Ginny was dating Wee,
I would have stopped her.

123
00:13:46,659 --> 00:13:50,904
He's a well-known player.

124
00:13:50,904 --> 00:13:55,187
Weechai and Weechana are half-siblings.

125
00:13:55,187 --> 00:14:01,624
People my age know it well
how dangerous the Chaichana family can be.

126
00:14:01,624 --> 00:14:05,920
Back then,
Weechai's mother disappeared without a trace.

127
00:14:05,920 --> 00:14:08,179
If you continue to date him,

128
00:14:08,179 --> 00:14:10,960
I think you need to be cautious.

129
00:14:31,896 --> 00:14:33,720
You should have told me you were coming,

130
00:14:33,720 --> 00:14:37,120
so I could prepare
something delicious for you.

131
00:14:37,803 --> 00:14:39,211
I don't want you to be too tired.

132
00:14:39,211 --> 00:14:42,816
No, I won't. I cook every day.

133
00:14:42,816 --> 00:14:45,040
Come on, honey. Let's go inside.

134
00:14:46,248 --> 00:14:48,184
Are you hungry?

135
00:14:48,184 --> 00:14:50,371
Let's go inside.

136
00:14:50,371 --> 00:14:52,480
Did you eat something?

137
00:15:05,808 --> 00:15:08,965
Here it is, your favorite dessert.

138
00:15:08,965 --> 00:15:12,240
Let's eat.

139
00:15:18,421 --> 00:15:19,929
You want me to feed you?

140
00:15:21,804 --> 00:15:26,760
Oh my! You cheeky girl!

141
00:15:27,578 --> 00:15:31,363
You work in action films,

142
00:15:31,363 --> 00:15:34,696
but the moment you come home,
you ask me to feed you.

143
00:15:34,696 --> 00:15:36,314
Oh my!

144
00:15:37,464 --> 00:15:39,640
Here.

145
00:15:43,899 --> 00:15:45,760
Is it good?

146
00:15:57,608 --> 00:15:59,214
Are you tired?

147
00:16:08,407 --> 00:16:10,542
What is going on?

148
00:16:10,542 --> 00:16:13,320
Who hurt you?

149
00:16:21,176 --> 00:16:22,590
What?

150
00:16:24,067 --> 00:16:25,757
It's okay.

151
00:16:25,757 --> 00:16:29,280
It's okay. It's gonna be okay.

152
00:16:30,872 --> 00:16:32,750
It's okay, I'm right here.

153
00:16:32,750 --> 00:16:34,311
It's okay.

154
00:16:41,499 --> 00:16:43,760
You will be okay.

155
00:16:56,875 --> 00:16:58,800
What is going on?

156
00:16:59,622 --> 00:17:02,029
I've never seen you cry like this.

157
00:17:02,029 --> 00:17:04,352
Who hurt you?

158
00:17:04,352 --> 00:17:06,584
I've decided to break up with Wee.

159
00:17:06,584 --> 00:17:10,702
Good for you! Thank you for doing this.

160
00:17:10,702 --> 00:17:13,528
You will finally be out of his circle.

161
00:17:13,528 --> 00:17:17,971
You won't find happiness dating a politician.

162
00:17:17,971 --> 00:17:20,456
True, he's wealthy,

163
00:17:20,456 --> 00:17:24,480
but I'm sure it comes with a price.

164
00:17:27,976 --> 00:17:31,020
Why did you decide to break up with him?

165
00:17:41,208 --> 00:17:44,904
We are not going to make it.

166
00:17:45,889 --> 00:17:47,818
His family won't accept me.

167
00:17:50,680 --> 00:17:52,856
And he has someone else.

168
00:17:53,757 --> 00:17:59,280
Good for you! You made the right choice.

169
00:18:00,072 --> 00:18:03,070
You need to be with someone
who appreciates your true value.

170
00:18:03,070 --> 00:18:05,280
If he doesn't appreciate you,
you need to leave.

171
00:18:06,635 --> 00:18:12,382
Look at me,
if I closed my shop for even a day,

172
00:18:12,382 --> 00:18:15,230
our neighbors wouldn't have anything to eat.

173
00:18:15,230 --> 00:18:18,278
I can't live anywhere else.

174
00:18:18,278 --> 00:18:24,040
You need to be in a place
where people will appreciate you.

175
00:18:29,055 --> 00:18:32,785
If nobody loves you, I still love you.

176
00:18:50,203 --> 00:18:51,819
Hey, Auntie.

177
00:18:53,462 --> 00:18:58,680
I may not be able to see you for a while.

178
00:19:00,187 --> 00:19:04,798
I need to practice my fighting
and English-speaking skills.

179
00:19:04,798 --> 00:19:07,190
Please take care of yourself.

180
00:19:07,190 --> 00:19:09,259
If you're too exhausted, you need to rest.

181
00:19:09,259 --> 00:19:11,400
If you need some sleep, you need to get some.

182
00:19:12,091 --> 00:19:16,040
You have money to spend,
so you don't have to be busy all the time.

183
00:19:19,753 --> 00:19:24,532
You need to say it to the girl in the mirror.

184
00:19:36,900 --> 00:19:38,865
I want to be good in what I do.

185
00:19:40,755 --> 00:19:43,680
You are already good in what you do.

186
00:19:51,341 --> 00:19:53,667
I want to be the Number 1 superstar.

187
00:19:53,667 --> 00:19:55,422
Sure, you can.

188
00:19:55,422 --> 00:19:58,360
Yes, you can, and you will.

189
00:19:58,360 --> 00:20:00,161
You're my superstar.

190
00:20:18,728 --> 00:20:20,328
Hello.

191
00:20:20,328 --> 00:20:23,870
Eva, can I see you for a bit?

192
00:20:23,870 --> 00:20:27,368
I don't like it that we argued.

193
00:20:27,368 --> 00:20:29,819
I don't think I can see you.

194
00:20:29,819 --> 00:20:31,229
Why's that?

195
00:20:33,062 --> 00:20:37,320
I feel a little bit under the weather.
I feel like I'm having a fever.

196
00:20:38,807 --> 00:20:42,400
Sure, if you say so.

197
00:20:42,400 --> 00:20:45,520
You should get some rest first.

198
00:20:45,520 --> 00:20:47,002
I understand.

199
00:20:54,923 --> 00:20:56,486
Sir?

200
00:20:56,486 --> 00:21:02,448
Are you going to ask Eva and Pie
to help you out with your campaign?

201
00:21:02,448 --> 00:21:03,798
That's right.

202
00:21:03,798 --> 00:21:07,842
Do you know about Pie and her friends' rate
for the event?

203
00:21:09,510 --> 00:21:11,311
I'll handle it.

204
00:21:12,171 --> 00:21:14,406
You need to ask the locals,

205
00:21:14,406 --> 00:21:16,425
ask them if they can help us in any way.

206
00:21:16,425 --> 00:21:18,226
Yes, sir.

207
00:21:35,483 --> 00:21:37,351
Eva.

208
00:21:38,603 --> 00:21:41,000
Where have you been?

209
00:21:43,053 --> 00:21:44,854
I went to see my aunt.

210
00:21:46,248 --> 00:21:50,958
Why didn't you tell me?
I called you, but you didn't answer.

211
00:21:50,958 --> 00:21:53,139
I'm sorry.

212
00:21:53,139 --> 00:21:56,120
I had a lot on my mind,
and I just ended up driving to her place.

213
00:21:57,875 --> 00:22:00,200
So he really was dating Ginny?

214
00:22:02,646 --> 00:22:04,284
Yeah.

215
00:22:08,326 --> 00:22:10,127
I've decided to break up with Wee.

216
00:22:14,216 --> 00:22:17,785
Honestly, I kinda knew
that he probably was dating someone else too,

217
00:22:17,785 --> 00:22:20,600
judging from the circle that he was in.

218
00:22:22,246 --> 00:22:24,280
I'm not okay about this.

219
00:22:25,323 --> 00:22:30,779
I'm not okay,
that he was dating Ginny or someone else.

220
00:22:32,253 --> 00:22:35,642
I'm fine if we use the same makeup artist.

221
00:22:36,955 --> 00:22:39,862
But I'm not okay
if we have the same boyfriend.

222
00:22:45,643 --> 00:22:47,640
And I'm tired.

223
00:22:49,419 --> 00:22:52,280
I'm tired of feeling
that I can never be good enough.

224
00:22:54,488 --> 00:22:57,000
He's not worth my effort.

225
00:22:59,721 --> 00:23:01,481
But he...

226
00:23:03,916 --> 00:23:05,849
he isn't loyal to me.

227
00:23:06,928 --> 00:23:08,769
Good.

228
00:23:08,769 --> 00:23:11,440
Cut him out of your life completely.

229
00:23:12,902 --> 00:23:15,960
When will you let him know?

230
00:23:20,720 --> 00:23:22,640
As soon as possible.

231
00:23:23,867 --> 00:23:26,400
I want to focus on my work.

232
00:23:27,664 --> 00:23:30,726
I hope that my work will turn out great.

233
00:23:30,726 --> 00:23:32,527
And I want to do this for myself.

234
00:23:35,760 --> 00:23:41,831
I want people to say
that the role that I got is made just for me,

235
00:23:42,560 --> 00:23:46,840
and that nobody can play this role but me.

236
00:23:48,166 --> 00:23:50,235
Of course, you can do it.

237
00:23:50,235 --> 00:23:52,283
You can do it.

238
00:23:54,120 --> 00:23:57,200
If you feel like this is too much for you,
you need to tell me.

239
00:24:25,544 --> 00:24:27,603
Thank you.

240
00:24:27,603 --> 00:24:29,390
- Yo!
- Yo!

241
00:24:29,390 --> 00:24:30,867
- Ready?
- Ready.

242
00:24:30,867 --> 00:24:32,072
Are you?

243
00:24:32,072 --> 00:24:33,374
Ready.

244
00:24:33,374 --> 00:24:36,504
Okay, we'll focus on running at zone 2 pace.

245
00:24:36,504 --> 00:24:38,440
So it won't be too exhausting for us.

246
00:24:39,704 --> 00:24:41,448
Okay, then.

247
00:24:41,448 --> 00:24:42,981
Shall we?

248
00:24:43,845 --> 00:24:45,356
Meaning?

249
00:24:46,510 --> 00:24:49,795
- Follow.
- What does it mean? Tell me!

250
00:24:49,795 --> 00:24:51,614
Hurry.

251
00:24:51,614 --> 00:24:52,998
Hurry.

252
00:24:52,998 --> 00:24:55,320
- Come on.
- What did you say?

253
00:24:56,075 --> 00:24:59,600
You use "Shall we?" when you invite someone
to do something with you.

254
00:24:59,600 --> 00:25:01,499
Like, "Shall we go?" or "Shall we dance?"

255
00:25:01,499 --> 00:25:03,560
You can also say,

256
00:25:03,560 --> 00:25:06,744
"Would you like to?" or, "How about we?"

257
00:25:06,744 --> 00:25:08,430
Or "Wanna go?",

258
00:25:08,430 --> 00:25:11,600
or something else simple as "We move?"

259
00:25:14,720 --> 00:25:16,306
You need to look at the context and situation

260
00:25:16,307 --> 00:25:18,600
when somebody asks you as well.

261
00:25:18,600 --> 00:25:23,123
If there're only just the two of you
and they ask, "Wanna go?"

262
00:25:23,123 --> 00:25:26,819
You should ask them back, "Wanna go do what?"

263
00:25:26,819 --> 00:25:28,632
"Do what exactly?"

264
00:25:28,632 --> 00:25:31,840
Because the unclear invitation
could lead to...

265
00:25:31,840 --> 00:25:33,742
something that is unhealthy.

266
00:25:33,742 --> 00:25:36,120
Oh, I got it.

267
00:25:36,851 --> 00:25:40,275
Like go partying? Or doing drugs?

268
00:25:40,275 --> 00:25:42,520
Or sleeping together, right?

269
00:25:43,400 --> 00:25:45,962
Yeah, something like that.

270
00:25:47,040 --> 00:25:48,841
Wanna go?

271
00:25:49,552 --> 00:25:51,009
Yes.

272
00:25:55,400 --> 00:26:00,168
This is a river, Chao Phraya.

273
00:26:00,168 --> 00:26:02,696
This is the Chao Phraya River.

274
00:26:02,696 --> 00:26:04,235
You need to say the specific name first.

275
00:26:04,235 --> 00:26:07,947
"River" only indicates what the place is,
like "street".

276
00:26:07,947 --> 00:26:12,006
When you want to say the place,
you need to say its name first.

277
00:26:12,006 --> 00:26:15,275
So it will be Chao Phraya River.

278
00:26:15,275 --> 00:26:17,094
Like "Sukhumvit" and followed by "Street".

279
00:26:17,094 --> 00:26:18,816
The way you say it will be different
from how you say it in Thai.

280
00:26:18,816 --> 00:26:20,798
Gosh, so confusing.

281
00:26:20,798 --> 00:26:23,851
Take your time, you don't need to rush.

282
00:26:23,851 --> 00:26:27,443
Also, when you're talking about places,

283
00:26:27,443 --> 00:26:30,819
you need to use "the", not "a".

284
00:26:30,819 --> 00:26:32,620
The...

285
00:26:34,181 --> 00:26:36,170
It's confusing.

286
00:26:36,170 --> 00:26:37,971
Take it slow.

287
00:26:43,124 --> 00:26:45,385
This is the...

288
00:26:46,619 --> 00:26:48,750
The... what is it called?

289
00:26:48,750 --> 00:26:50,600
Small river.

290
00:26:50,600 --> 00:26:54,192
Close. We would call this "a canal".

291
00:26:54,192 --> 00:26:57,040
A river is a natural stream of water.

292
00:26:57,040 --> 00:26:59,360
When it is a man-made constructed water way,

293
00:26:59,360 --> 00:27:03,000
we'd call this "a canal", not small river.

294
00:27:03,819 --> 00:27:05,190
Kaa-nal.

295
00:27:05,190 --> 00:27:06,976
- Try again?
- Canal.

296
00:27:06,976 --> 00:27:08,678
It's pretty good.

297
00:27:08,678 --> 00:27:10,479
Canal.

298
00:27:16,120 --> 00:27:18,410
You speak Thai quite fluently.

299
00:27:19,379 --> 00:27:21,800
I lived in Thailand until I was 16 years old.

300
00:27:22,419 --> 00:27:24,179
My parents were in a car accident.

301
00:27:24,179 --> 00:27:26,459
I had no one left but my uncle
who lived abroad.

302
00:27:26,459 --> 00:27:28,560
So I needed to move there to live with him.

303
00:27:29,536 --> 00:27:31,804
My dad left my mom.

304
00:27:33,403 --> 00:27:38,816
After that, she passed away,
so I lived with my aunt.

305
00:27:38,816 --> 00:27:41,353
I grew up with her street food business.

306
00:27:42,224 --> 00:27:44,320
And I grew up in my uncle's kitchen.

307
00:27:46,859 --> 00:27:48,976
Excuse me.

308
00:27:48,976 --> 00:27:50,600
- Oh my!
- It's her!

309
00:27:50,600 --> 00:27:52,167
- Can I take a picture with you?
- Okay.

310
00:27:52,167 --> 00:27:53,862
Sure.

311
00:27:53,862 --> 00:27:55,467
You're so pretty.

312
00:27:55,467 --> 00:27:58,014
One... two... three.

313
00:27:58,014 --> 00:28:00,560
You're not in the frame.

314
00:28:01,374 --> 00:28:03,283
Can you take one for us?

315
00:28:03,283 --> 00:28:04,632
- Take a picture for us?
- Right.

316
00:28:04,632 --> 00:28:07,880
- Sure.
- Please get a wide shot.

317
00:28:07,880 --> 00:28:10,080
Sure, got it.

318
00:28:12,240 --> 00:28:15,200
Three... two... one.

319
00:28:15,200 --> 00:28:16,307
Alright.

320
00:28:16,307 --> 00:28:17,320
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

321
00:28:17,320 --> 00:28:18,803
Can I check them first?

322
00:28:18,803 --> 00:28:20,606
- I want to know if they look great.
- So great.

323
00:28:20,606 --> 00:28:24,440
- Eva, can we take a picture with you?
- Sure.

324
00:28:29,352 --> 00:28:31,400
- Take one for me.
- Sure.

325
00:28:31,400 --> 00:28:33,014
I'm still working out,
so I can't stay for long.

326
00:28:33,014 --> 00:28:34,627
Can you all get in one frame?

327
00:28:34,627 --> 00:28:36,428
I don't want to upset my personal trainer.

328
00:28:39,768 --> 00:28:41,569
Ready?

329
00:28:42,336 --> 00:28:44,160
Thank you.

330
00:28:45,360 --> 00:28:46,887
Thank you.

331
00:28:58,123 --> 00:29:00,203
Hello.

332
00:29:00,203 --> 00:29:02,080
Hey.

333
00:29:02,080 --> 00:29:03,851
You're so cute.

334
00:29:03,851 --> 00:29:05,840
I'm running on my treadmill tomorrow.

335
00:29:07,222 --> 00:29:10,017
I didn't expect so many people
would come to you.

336
00:29:10,017 --> 00:29:12,520
See? I told you.

337
00:29:13,782 --> 00:29:15,499
Why are you laughing? What did I say wrong?

338
00:29:15,499 --> 00:29:19,625
Nope, it's great. You said it right.

339
00:29:19,625 --> 00:29:20,945
Here.

340
00:29:24,016 --> 00:29:26,120
Good job, let's go.

341
00:29:36,448 --> 00:29:39,027
<i>I met Eva during my morning run.</i>

342
00:29:39,027 --> 00:29:41,603
Huh? What's this?

343
00:29:41,603 --> 00:29:44,419
<i>I just died! I got to run close to Eva.</i>

344
00:29:44,419 --> 00:29:46,563
<i>Eva is so cute.</i>

345
00:29:46,563 --> 00:29:48,846
<i>Who is there with her? He's so hot.</i>

346
00:29:48,846 --> 00:29:50,814
<i>Whoa! Who is running with Eva?</i>

347
00:29:50,814 --> 00:29:52,830
<i>This is not the guy she dated with.</i>

348
00:29:52,830 --> 00:29:54,510
<i>He's so hot, is he her personal trainer?</i>

349
00:29:54,510 --> 00:29:55,923
<i>I like their chemistry.</i>

350
00:29:55,923 --> 00:29:58,587
<i>Can I get his Instagram?</i>

351
00:29:58,587 --> 00:30:01,083
Oh, please people!
Stop your imagination right now.

352
00:30:01,083 --> 00:30:03,684
We don't want to be in trouble.

353
00:30:05,088 --> 00:30:06,128
Hey!

354
00:30:06,128 --> 00:30:07,395
Eva, get in the car!

355
00:30:07,395 --> 00:30:08,475
- Hurry!
- Where are we going?

356
00:30:08,475 --> 00:30:09,600
I need to stretch first.

357
00:30:09,600 --> 00:30:13,822
No need to. You need to go, now.

358
00:30:13,822 --> 00:30:17,280
- What is going on?
- Pun, get in.

359
00:30:18,352 --> 00:30:20,560
- What is wrong with you?
- Just get in.

360
00:30:20,560 --> 00:30:23,300
What? I'm starting to get mad.

361
00:30:32,483 --> 00:30:34,422
I was so busy

362
00:30:34,422 --> 00:30:35,399
that I forgot

363
00:30:35,400 --> 00:30:38,080
that you two shouldn't be
going out and jogging like this.

364
00:30:38,798 --> 00:30:41,475
They posted it up so quickly.

365
00:30:41,475 --> 00:30:44,019
What music did they play in the background?

366
00:30:44,019 --> 00:30:45,820
What is going on?

367
00:30:47,571 --> 00:30:49,390
People posted about us jogging in the park.

368
00:30:50,155 --> 00:30:51,956
What?

369
00:30:53,019 --> 00:30:55,344
You can't jog outside anymore.

370
00:30:55,344 --> 00:30:56,707
If you want to jog outside,

371
00:30:56,707 --> 00:30:59,400
I need to go with you,
or someone else needs to.

372
00:31:00,304 --> 00:31:03,286
They are breaking the law.

373
00:31:03,286 --> 00:31:05,974
I mean, they invaded our privacy.

374
00:31:05,974 --> 00:31:07,775
We can't normalize this.

375
00:31:08,566 --> 00:31:12,256
Welcome to my life.
I can't do anything about it.

376
00:31:12,256 --> 00:31:14,347
Really?

377
00:31:14,347 --> 00:31:17,216
I'll tell you about it when we're at the gym.

378
00:31:17,216 --> 00:31:20,200
About what to do, and what not to do
when you're around Eva.

379
00:31:32,443 --> 00:31:33,817
Who is he?

380
00:31:39,488 --> 00:31:41,536
Her personal trainer.

381
00:31:41,536 --> 00:31:44,280
He was the one
who saved her from the stalker.

382
00:31:44,998 --> 00:31:49,258
You need to warn her
not to let it happen again.

383
00:31:50,790 --> 00:31:55,662
People won't focus on our campaign
when there's news like this.

384
00:31:55,662 --> 00:32:00,188
I need people to focus
mainly on our campaign, okay?

385
00:32:02,035 --> 00:32:03,484
Got it.

386
00:32:07,720 --> 00:32:11,191
Wee, we need to talk.

387
00:32:28,880 --> 00:32:30,681
Did you see it?

388
00:32:32,491 --> 00:32:34,438
I saw it.

389
00:32:34,438 --> 00:32:37,267
Did she intentionally do that
because she was mad at you?

390
00:32:37,267 --> 00:32:39,395
She didn't respect you at all.

391
00:32:39,395 --> 00:32:41,838
Who's the guy?

392
00:32:41,838 --> 00:32:43,235
Her personal trainer.

393
00:32:43,235 --> 00:32:45,976
I think he was training her
according to the program.

394
00:32:45,976 --> 00:32:49,584
I was about to talk to her about it myself.

395
00:32:49,584 --> 00:32:50,679
But Dad said

396
00:32:50,680 --> 00:32:53,195
that I needed to wait
until campaigning is over.

397
00:32:53,195 --> 00:32:57,066
Is she that important?
You can't find someone else?

398
00:32:57,066 --> 00:33:02,019
Everything is included
in the campaign planning already.

399
00:33:02,019 --> 00:33:05,960
Our research team sees
that it will benefit us.

400
00:33:05,960 --> 00:33:08,628
When we invited her
for the CSR event earlier,

401
00:33:08,628 --> 00:33:13,491
it increased satisfied engagement
from our target household group.

402
00:33:13,491 --> 00:33:18,880
Does she know how to behave appropriately?

403
00:33:21,107 --> 00:33:23,440
I will talk to her about it.

404
00:33:29,040 --> 00:33:31,280
You need to take care of it.

405
00:33:31,280 --> 00:33:33,395
After the election,

406
00:33:33,395 --> 00:33:35,665
you need to break up with her immediately.

407
00:33:39,396 --> 00:33:41,197
Do you hear me?

408
00:33:43,011 --> 00:33:44,630
Loud and clear.

409
00:33:56,320 --> 00:33:59,040
[Ruam Thai Chana]

410
00:34:05,910 --> 00:34:08,200
You have interviews

411
00:34:08,200 --> 00:34:11,106
with two famous online magazines
this afternoon.

412
00:34:11,106 --> 00:34:14,005
And the press conference of the campaign
is in the evening.

413
00:34:14,005 --> 00:34:16,920
Reporters from all channels
will be joining the event.

414
00:34:17,830 --> 00:34:21,942
Can you tell one of our reporters
to ask about Eva?

415
00:34:21,942 --> 00:34:24,560
Sure. What topic will it be about, sir?

416
00:34:24,560 --> 00:34:27,768
About her jogging with a guy this morning.

417
00:34:28,627 --> 00:34:29,280
But sir...

418
00:34:29,280 --> 00:34:33,857
Tell them to ask me
about how I felt when I saw the clips.

419
00:34:35,184 --> 00:34:38,659
I'll tell them that I trust her

420
00:34:38,659 --> 00:34:41,655
even though we are having some personal issues
at the moment.

421
00:34:41,655 --> 00:34:46,691
They need to ask a follow-up question,
about the personal issues.

422
00:34:46,691 --> 00:34:49,328
So I can say
that I'm too dedicated to my work,

423
00:34:49,328 --> 00:34:52,141
and I have neglected people
who are close to me.

424
00:34:52,141 --> 00:34:54,381
After that, there will be no more questions.

425
00:34:54,381 --> 00:34:57,456
Got it, sir. I will take care of it.

426
00:35:16,800 --> 00:35:18,079
[Pathumwan Metropolis Police Station]

427
00:35:18,080 --> 00:35:20,120
[Police]

428
00:35:21,315 --> 00:35:23,133
Sir?

429
00:35:23,133 --> 00:35:25,291
What's up?

430
00:35:25,291 --> 00:35:26,875
Can you buy me a cup of coffee?

431
00:35:28,826 --> 00:35:30,309
Let's go.

432
00:35:31,990 --> 00:35:35,987
My friend asked me to tell you this.

433
00:35:37,240 --> 00:35:39,371
Ginny was drugged.

434
00:35:39,371 --> 00:35:41,920
The reporter was also drugged
with the same drug last year.

435
00:35:43,035 --> 00:35:44,790
It's the same type of drug.

436
00:35:44,790 --> 00:35:46,771
Minimal use.

437
00:35:46,771 --> 00:35:50,400
But they don't know the ingredients.
They're waiting for the lab result.

438
00:35:51,136 --> 00:35:54,517
My friend from the forensic team said

439
00:35:54,517 --> 00:35:57,920
that the symptoms should be
shortness of breath and foaming at the mouth.

440
00:35:57,920 --> 00:36:02,968
Her bleeding should be
from contaminated chemicals left in her body.

441
00:36:04,086 --> 00:36:06,926
What about the stalker that attacked Eva?

442
00:36:06,926 --> 00:36:09,280
- He was released.
- What?

443
00:36:11,000 --> 00:36:12,669
You didn't know?

444
00:36:12,669 --> 00:36:14,995
We confiscated his computer and hard disk.

445
00:36:14,995 --> 00:36:17,597
He paid the maximum fine and got released.

446
00:36:17,597 --> 00:36:20,445
Where are the confiscated items?

447
00:36:20,445 --> 00:36:22,269
In the evidence room.

448
00:36:22,269 --> 00:36:24,070
Are you sure?

449
00:36:26,337 --> 00:36:29,475
I'm not sure about that.

450
00:36:29,475 --> 00:36:32,000
The cases were closed in strange way...

451
00:36:32,781 --> 00:36:34,995
Both Ginny and the stalker's cases.

452
00:36:36,014 --> 00:36:39,867
I heard that there were video clips

453
00:36:39,867 --> 00:36:44,069
of Ginny getting cozy
with the new party's leader,

454
00:36:44,069 --> 00:36:45,397
who is Eva's boyfriend.

455
00:36:45,397 --> 00:36:47,440
It happened before the election.

456
00:36:48,662 --> 00:36:50,463
What do you think?

457
00:36:56,806 --> 00:36:59,987
Okay, two minutes easy,
one minute hard, okay?

458
00:36:59,987 --> 00:37:01,889
Two minutes slow, one minute fast.

459
00:37:01,889 --> 00:37:04,082
Then we alternate, okay?

460
00:37:05,648 --> 00:37:08,608
Hey, I can't take it.

461
00:37:08,608 --> 00:37:11,152
I know it's tiring, but this is the last set.

462
00:37:11,152 --> 00:37:12,953
Come on, let's go.

463
00:37:16,072 --> 00:37:18,073
Okay.

464
00:37:18,073 --> 00:37:20,320
That's enough, good job.

465
00:37:22,400 --> 00:37:23,989
Let's stretch.

466
00:37:47,984 --> 00:37:49,792
Don't forget to get some protein.

467
00:37:49,792 --> 00:37:52,614
You need it to repair your muscles.

468
00:37:52,614 --> 00:37:57,168
I might need to read the script
and send it to the producer next week.

469
00:37:57,168 --> 00:38:00,117
You got this. You will do great, I'm sure.

470
00:38:00,117 --> 00:38:02,667
Boat will be taking off his cast tomorrow.

471
00:38:02,667 --> 00:38:04,680
Then I can tutor you full time.

472
00:38:05,680 --> 00:38:10,536
You can leave if you want to.
Domino will be here soon.

473
00:38:10,536 --> 00:38:11,903
Okay.

474
00:38:31,374 --> 00:38:33,917
What are you doing here?

475
00:38:33,917 --> 00:38:35,859
I called you so many times.

476
00:38:35,859 --> 00:38:39,320
You never answered
or returned any of my calls.

477
00:38:40,243 --> 00:38:42,591
You were training that hard?

478
00:38:43,400 --> 00:38:44,520
This is my job.

479
00:38:44,520 --> 00:38:45,959
I know.

480
00:38:46,803 --> 00:38:49,987
I'm not disturbing you.
I'm just worried about you.

481
00:38:50,675 --> 00:38:52,880
Actually, I've been here for a while.

482
00:38:52,880 --> 00:38:56,360
I tried to call you
and you didn't pick up your phone.

483
00:38:57,776 --> 00:39:00,619
Let me give you a ride, come on.

484
00:39:00,619 --> 00:39:01,957
It's okay.

485
00:39:01,957 --> 00:39:04,760
- Domino will be here soon.
- Tell her to leave.

486
00:39:07,003 --> 00:39:09,720
Hey, you! You need to leave.

487
00:39:10,411 --> 00:39:11,816
Wee.

488
00:39:11,816 --> 00:39:13,617
What's the matter?

489
00:39:15,817 --> 00:39:18,446
- Get in the car.
- You can't do this to me.

490
00:39:18,446 --> 00:39:20,222
I will show you what I can do.

491
00:39:20,222 --> 00:39:22,640
- Come here.
- Let me go!

492
00:39:34,104 --> 00:39:36,579
Hey! Stop! Stop!

493
00:39:36,579 --> 00:39:39,214
- What is going on?
- Stop!

494
00:39:39,214 --> 00:39:42,001
What is going on? Pun!

495
00:39:42,001 --> 00:39:45,000
- Wee!
- Wee, you need to stop!

496
00:39:45,840 --> 00:39:48,107
Can't you leave her in peace
for just one day?

497
00:39:48,107 --> 00:39:50,480
Why do you need to get physical with him?

498
00:39:53,088 --> 00:39:54,502
- What? What?
- Wee!

499
00:39:54,502 --> 00:39:56,523
Pun! Pun!

500
00:39:56,523 --> 00:39:58,566
Please, I beg you.

501
00:40:00,112 --> 00:40:02,288
Let him go.

502
00:40:02,288 --> 00:40:04,089
Assholes!

503
00:40:05,483 --> 00:40:07,284
Damn it!

504
00:40:11,077 --> 00:40:12,360
Asshole!

505
00:40:12,360 --> 00:40:14,200
Damn it!

506
00:40:14,200 --> 00:40:16,572
How the hell was I supposed to know, dude?

507
00:40:17,778 --> 00:40:20,938
I heard you just got back
from overseas, didn't you?

508
00:40:22,267 --> 00:40:24,600
- Yeah.
- From where?

509
00:40:24,600 --> 00:40:27,600
- From New York, sir.
- New York, I see.

